    "nw_faq_3DEjy9": {
      "type": "nw-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_yQLT8W": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes Ultimate Snooze different from traditional mattresses?",
            "answer": "<p>Most conventional mattresses rely on polyurethane foams, synthetic adhesives, and various fire-barrier materials. Ultimate Snooze takes a different approach, using certified organic cotton, organic wool, natural latex, and supportive pocketed coils. Our mattresses are handcrafted in the USA without polyurethane foam, fiberglass, or chemical flame retardants and developed in collaboration with Gary Brecka.</p><h3></h3>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Tz3QdY": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why should I care about what's inside my mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>You spend nearly one-third of your life in bed, yet most people never question what their mattress is made of. Some conventional mattresses contain petroleum-based foams, adhesives, and synthetic materials that can release volatile organic compounds (VOCs). Ultimate Snooze focuses on breathable natural materials and removing unnecessary synthetic components from your sleep environment.</p><h3></h3>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nJerdq": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will an organic mattress help me sleep cooler?",
            "answer": "<p>Our mattresses are designed for natural breathability. Organic wool helps manage moisture, cotton allows airflow, and natural latex offers a more open, responsive feel than many dense memory foams. Together, these materials help reduce heat buildup for a more comfortable sleep environment.</p><h3></h3>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_YzpH4U": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I don't love my mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>All Mattresses have a 100-night trial which means you can try the mattress at home for 100-nights and return it for a refund if you do not like it. All mattresses are backed by s limited 30-year warranty.&nbsp;</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_7wJtPr": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What payment options are available? (FSA/HSA, Financing)",
            "answer": "<p>We offer flexible financing through Affirm, allowing eligible customers to spread payments over time. Select mattress purchases may also qualify for HSA/FSA reimbursement, depending on eligibility and your plan's requirements.</p><h3></h3>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_f3ELhf": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why did Gary Brecka partner with Ultimate Snooze?",
            "answer": "<p>After years studying human health and recovery, Gary Brecka began questioning the materials people sleep on every night. His search for an organic mattress without conventional synthetic foams and unnecessary chemical additives led him to partner with Matt Smith of Snooze Mattress Company. Together, they developed a recovery-focused mattress collection built around certified organic materials and a cleaner sleep environment.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
